# Developer 1 — Core platform

## Owns

Auth, goals, tasks, overview, calendar data, integrations catalog/connect API surface, Postgres models/migrations, seed catalog, frontend Import/Goals/Overview repository wiring.

## Allowed paths

- `backend/app/api/auth.py`, `goals.py`, `tasks.py`, `sources.py`, `integrations.py`, `overview.py`
- `backend/app/services/auth_service.py`, `goal_service.py`, `task_service.py`, `source_service.py`, `overview_service.py`, `activity_service.py`, `seed_data.py`, `seed_db.py`, `runtime_store.py`
- `backend/app/models/`, `backend/app/schemas/`, `backend/alembic/`, `backend/tests/`
- `frontend/src/shared/js/api/`, `frontend/src/shared/js/repositories/`
- `frontend/src/pages/overview/`, `frontend/src/pages/goals/`, `frontend/src/pages/import-data/`

## Forbidden

- `backend/app/adapters/` (Dev2)
- `backend/app/services/agent_service.py`, `memory_service.py`, `mcp_service.py`, `messaging_service.py` (Dev2 implements; Dev1 only calls them)
- Implementing Nango/AstrBot/Harness/TencentDB clients — including the body of `auth_connector.py`. Dev1 owns that *interface*; Dev2 owns the Nango implementation behind it.
- A second Goals/Use agent loop
- Collaboration/social endpoints

## Integration rules

Call Dev2 through interfaces only:

- `AuthConnector` for Nango OAuth
- `MessagingService.connect_platform` for AstrBot
- `MCPService.register_connection` / `unregister` after connect/revoke

Adding a connector is a catalog row (`auth_type` + optional `nango_provider_key`), not a new router.
